pipette-scores — third-party attribution

This repository bundles and adapts third-party code. Full license texts are in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

Vendored verbatim
- vendor/ifbench — the upstream IFBench repository, from allenai/IFBench
  (Apache-2.0), vendored as a git submodule (LICENSE at vendor/ifbench/LICENSE).
  Only its test set is used.
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/asr/open_asr_normalizer/ — the Open
  ASR Leaderboard's English text normalizer (normalizer.py, english_abbreviations.py),
  from huggingface/open_asr_leaderboard @ 67e8bd6acea240819ad67080f6f31e15d4a90da5
  (Apache-2.0, (c) 2022 The OpenAI team and The HuggingFace Team; mostly copied, per
  its header, from openai/whisper, MIT, (c) 2022 OpenAI), and its multilingual
  normalizer and compound-pair alignment (multilingual.py: unchanged excerpts of
  normalizer/data_utils.py and normalizer/eval_utils.py @
  62a457c5c32d0de4df77e9470308aae7d45b055f, Apache-2.0).
  Provenance and hashes of the ASR files: scoring/asr/NOTICE.md.

Vendored with modifications
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/math_500/prm800k/grading/ — the PRM800K
  mathematical equivalence grader (grader.py, math_normalize.py), from openai/prm800k
  (MIT, (c) 2023 OpenAI). The changes are a relative import and raw-string regex
  literals; the behavior is the same. Its __init__.py is Liquid AI's. Its
  math_normalize.py is, per its header, largely copied from Hendrycks' MATH
  `math_equivalence` (hendrycks/math, MIT, (c) 2021 Dan Hendrycks).
- vendor/ifbench-checkers — the IFBench scoring source (evaluation_lib.py,
  instructions.py, instructions_registry.py, instructions_util.py), from
  allenai/IFBench @ 1a902f9 (Apache-2.0, (c) Allen Institute for AI and The Google
  Research Authors). Liquid AI changed instructions.py, instructions_util.py and
  evaluation_lib.py; each carries a notice, and the changes are listed in
  vendor/ifbench-checkers/README.md.
  At build time these files are bundled into the wheel under
  pipette_scores/scoring/ifbench/_upstream/ (including the LICENSE).

Adapted
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/dataset_catalog/_asr_audio.py —
  `resample_16k_mono` follows the decoding sequence of huggingface/datasets
  2.19.0's `Audio.decode_example` (Apache-2.0, (c) The HuggingFace Datasets
  Authors) and librosa's `to_mono`, `resample` (res_type "soxr_hq") and
  `util.fix_length` (librosa/librosa, ISC, (c) 2013--2026 librosa development team).
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/vlm_upstream/, scoring/profile_answers.py,
  dataset_catalog/prompt_profiles.py, dataset_catalog/_vlm_build.py and _vlm_common.py, and
  the seven VLM dataset builders in packages/pipette-scores/scripts/ — answer extraction and
  metrics, a model wrapper's answer extraction, model-specific prompts and the datasets'
  default prompts and pinned sources, from open-compass/VLMEvalKit @ 8eca8e5 (Apache-2.0,
  (c) 2023 VLMEvalKit Authors), modified by Liquid AI (deterministic only: no LLM judge, no
  random choice). Each file names what it ports; THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md lists them.
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/math_500/math_generic.py — the robust-boxed
  numeric normalization (`normalize_numeric_answer`) is copied from groq/openbench
  `robust_boxed.py` (MIT, (c) 2025 Groq, Inc.).

Liquid AI original work (extracted from the internal verifiers catalogue)
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/gpqa_diamond/mcq.py and the answer-extraction /
  orchestration in math_generic.py are Liquid AI's own clean-room implementation of
  the publicly described Artificial Analysis benchmarking methodology. Artificial
  Analysis publishes a methodology description, not source code; "AA" / "Artificial
  Analysis" references in the code denote that methodology, not any third-party code.
  This logic is fully owned by Liquid AI.

Liquid AI original work — vendored from a separate Liquid repo
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/ifstruct.py and the vendored
  `vendor/ifstruct` validator are Liquid AI's own (Liquid4All/ifstruct); they carry
  no third-party license and are covered by this repository's license.
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/math_500/liquid_evals_parser.py holds
  unchanged excerpts of Liquid AI's Liquid4All/liquid_evals (liquid_evals/parser.py
  @ d5534cf). Its sympy grader derives from openai/prm800k (MIT, (c) 2023 OpenAI)
  and its mathd normalization from hendrycks/math (MIT, (c) 2021 Dan Hendrycks);
  both licenses are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.
- packages/pipette-scores/pipette_scores/scoring/completion_text.py
  (`remove_thinking_tags`) is vendored from the same liquid_evals/parser.py.

